sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch11-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Based on flotation and germination experiments, the seeds of roughly 10 per cent of the plants of a flora, after drying, could be floated by sea currents across about 900 miles of sea and still germinate.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "About a tenth of a flora's seeds could survive sea-drift across 900 miles";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XI, “Geographical Distribution”; section “Means of dispersal, by changes of climate and of the level of the land, and by occasional means”. Scope: seeds and fruits of flowering plants exposed to sea-water"
}
